     shared account.

  3) Distribution inside an organisation: unmodified official installers may
     be distributed within an organisation (internal software repositories,
     intranet downloads, bulk deployment). Offering downloads or mirrors to
     the public requires the Author's prior written permission.

3. Prohibited without prior written permission

You may not:

  • Decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer VsTerm, or otherwise attempt to
    obtain its source code (except to the extent applicable law expressly
    permits this and does not allow it to be excluded by agreement);
  • Crack, bypass, disable or tamper with license checks, trial periods or Pro
    restrictions, or make or distribute tools, patches or key generators for
    that purpose;
  • Distribute modified installers or program files; repackage or rebrand for
    publication, sale, rental, subscription, or as part of a paid service;
  • Claim software copyright, patents, trademarks, domains, or other IP on
    modifications, derivatives, or wrappers based on this project;
  • Remove or alter this copyright / license notice;
  • Offer products or services in VsTerm's name or pose as official
    (describing, recommending and using VsTerm is fine).

4. Source code

The VsTerm source code is All Rights Reserved and not licensed to anyone.
Source the Author shares with specific people is for them to read, study or
contribute to development only, and grants no right to distribute it. Without
the Author's written permission you may not publish, distribute, or fork and
release the source, or integrate it in whole or in part into other projects
for external delivery.

5. Security research

Analysis needed to find, verify and report a security vulnerability to the
Author is not restricted by the first item of section 3, provided that:

  • you report it privately to the address below and do not disclose details
    before a fix is released; and
  • you do not use it to harm any user, to crack or bypass license
    restrictions, or to distribute cracked builds.

6. Third-party components

Open-source libraries and embedded fonts (e.g. JetBrains Mono, Noto Sans SC)
